From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Segno floor-console spike <to.sasovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: don't abort cursor plane assignment on non-shm buffers (RPi)

On the Raspberry Pi (vc4 / V3D KMS), drm_output_find_plane_for_view()
aborts the compositor when a cursor view reaches the plane switch with a
NULL shm_buffer. Turn the assert into a graceful continue so the view
falls through to GL renderer compositing instead of crashing the kiosk on
pointer input.

Rebased for weston 15 (wrynose); the weston 14 PRIMARY/OVERLAY asserts
this patch originally replaced are gone upstream.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hardware/config-specific workaround]

---
 libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c b/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/state-propose.c
@@ -655,7 +655,8 @@ drm_output_find_plane_for_view(struct drm_output_state *state,

 		switch (plane->type) {
 		case WDRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR:
-			assert(buffer->shm_buffer);
+			if (!buffer->shm_buffer)
+				continue;
 			assert(plane == output->cursor_plane);
 			break;
 		case WDRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY:
